WEBVTT

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.780
Wait up, Kozue!

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:50.050
Why the big hurry?
A date?

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:52.410
Wrong.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:58.850
That class was rough.
My shoulders are so stiff!

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.620
You're not kidding!
That prof tires me out.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.790
What do you say we
go to Harajuku?

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.330
Not me. That place is
for kids.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:08.770
Anyone want to get
a bite to eat?

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:12.140
Okay, follow me.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:13.430
You're treating?

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:14.600
A large parfait for me!

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:17.010
Don't be silly!
You pay your own.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:24.510
COFFEE SHOP
SCORPlON LEG LOCK

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:28.880
What?! You're kidding, right?
I can't believe that!

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:34.520
There you go again!
Everybody does it. Right?

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.160
Of course. Nothing to be
surprised about.

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:41.270
You have a boyfriend,
don't you, Kozue?

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.800
His name was...

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:44.900
Godai.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.940
Don't you take trips
together?

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:48.570
Oh no!

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:52.170
Haven't you been seeing
each other a long time?

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.070
How far along have you gotten?

00:02:55.450 --> 00:03:01.650
How far?
Godai isn't like that.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:03.820
He's a real gentleman.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.160
I can't believe I'm
hearing this!

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:09.500
So in your case, Kozue...

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.420
you've just held hands...

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:18.600
and let him put his arms around you?
That's the extent?

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:19.670
No.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:21.600
Not even that.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:22.500
Come on!

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:24.970
Something must be wrong
with the guy.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:26.650
There's nothing wrong
with him.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.240
I'll be frank.
He's not normal! Right?

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:31.550
I'd have to agree.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.250
That's not true!

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:38.990
Or is it?

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.600
Hi there, Godai!

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:57.130
How nice.
A date with Kozue?

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:58.560
Lady-killer!

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:03.930
Young Godai!

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.800
Better hurry before
the manager gets back.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:10.880
Then let go of my arm!

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:15.280
Will you treat me to
a deluxe tempura on rice?

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:18.320
Okay.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.990
Deluxe, now.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.150
I heard you the first time!

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.760
Don't forget my deluxe
tempura on rice.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:29.900
Forget it!

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:32.710
Where're you going?

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:36.200
Uh...out.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.400
You're weird.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:38.940
Let's go, Soichiro!

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:43.750
A date?

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:47.150
Your necktie's crooked.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:48.910
I wouldn't call it a date.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:51.880
Did I make it too tight?

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:54.360
N-No.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:57.820
There. That looks right.

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:00.760
Thanks.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:03.290
Have a good time.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:05.360
Have a good time!

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.240
Thanks! 'Bye!

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.220
Pigeons!

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:22.620
UEYAMA ZOO

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:39.960
Tigers!

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.300
Look, Godai, tigers!

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.520
They're not moving at all.

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:07.460
Godai.

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:10.660
Godai?

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:13.030
Godai, are you there?!

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:14.900
Huh? What?

00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:20.110
Did you call my name?

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.310
What's the matter, Godai?

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:26.010
You don't seem to be
enjoying yourself.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:28.480
Huh?

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:32.020
No, that's not true.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:35.250
Is your necktie bothering you?

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:37.060
My necktie?

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:42.800
Shall we get something
to drink?

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:55.150
Thank you very much.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:57.850
You're going to spill that!

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:04.550
Would you have preferred
a movie?

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:07.620
Oh no! This is lots
more fun!

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:08.860
Really?

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:10.860
Yes!

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:43.230
Godai! Come quick!

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:48.200
Look how big those carp are!

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:50.300
They're really huge.

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:52.400
Over there, too.

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:56.480
They must be on a date.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:08:59.410
It's time we headed home.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.820
Let's walk a little longer.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:10.010
But...it's time.

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:12.110
That's no fun.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:18.060
Why don't you come over
to my house for dinner!

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:21.030
No...thanks.

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:22.690
Why not?

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:27.230
I was over for dinner
just the other day.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:28.670
But...

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:45.160
I'm cold!

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:46.590
There you go,
a human heater.

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:51.150
You're so warm!

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:57.290
What's the matter, Kozue?

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:02.900
Oh, nothing.

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:11.950
Are you cold?

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.490
Yes, freezing!

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:20.720
Then let's go home.
You don't want to catch cold.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:41.110
NANAO

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:45.090
You should've invited
Godai over.

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:47.400
I did.

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:49.610
Why didn't he come?

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:53.360
I don't know.

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:56.560
He dumped you, Sis!

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.130
That hurts!
What's that for?

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:05.730
We're on very good terms.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:11.370
I hope you're both
behaving yourselves.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:12.510
What do you mean?

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:16.290
Godai is, after all
a Man.

00:11:20.590 --> 00:11:22.680
Don't read the paper
at the dinner table!

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.080
I'm not sure anymore!

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:48.000
This passage by the celebrated
French author, Edmond Rostand...

00:12:48.350 --> 00:12:52.370
is famous as the climactic
last scene of Cyrano de Bergerac.

00:12:52.990 --> 00:12:54.850
A scientist and a musician...

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:59.380
Cyrano was skilled with
both sword and pen.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:02.060
His prominent proboscis,
however...

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:05.620
forced him to give up
the love of his life.

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:09.090
Concealing the intense
love in his heart...

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:14.320
he penned letters from the
battlefield to his beloved Roxanne...

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:16.810
for Christian, a handsome
but illiterate fellow.

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:32.440
Straighten your elbow
a bit more.

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:36.360
The basics are very
important.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.190
Okay. Again.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:06.420
Thank you so much
for treating me!

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:09.820
Don't be bashful.
Order anything you'd like.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:11.990
I really shouldn't!

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:13.360
Go right ahead.

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:15.020
I shouldn't!

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.160
Cheesecake and English
tea with lemon.

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:20.360
Is that one of each?
Right away.

00:14:20.570 --> 00:14:21.790
Thanks!

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:24.610
You're always so cheerful.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:30.570
Actually, I'm depressed.

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:31.440
What?

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:34.000
I can't understand...

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:40.020
the way men feel.

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:44.050
Did something happen between
you and Godai?

00:14:44.930 --> 00:14:47.120
That's just it.
Nothing happened.

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:53.120
Is Godai in love with
someone?

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:55.670
So that's it.

00:14:56.410 --> 00:15:01.430
She doesn't know that Godai
likes Miss Otonoshi.

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:12.850
Love is a gamble.

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:16.860
You can be dating as friends
all along...

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:20.960
but the moment you mention
the word "love," it's over.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:24.400
If you hadn't said anything...

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:27.020
your relationship might've
gone on forever.

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:28.830
But...

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:33.570
Godai doesn't have the nerve.
It's as simple as that.

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:36.070
Do you really think so?

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:38.240
Sure.

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:48.180
It's getting cold.

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:51.650
Let's head back.

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:01.060
Forgive me!

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:02.030
No, that's all right!

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:05.330
I hope we can talk like
this again.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:08.870
Sure. You're welcome
to come anytime.

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:10.560
Really?!

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:12.340
That makes me so happy!

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:14.180
Now, shall we go home?

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:15.200
Okay!

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:31.130
I saw.

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:36.570
What?!

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.500
Coach Mitaka with Kozue?

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:44.010
They're an unlikely couple.

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:45.780
But it's a fact.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:49.240
Hey! What's going on?!

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:50.950
I-I...

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:53.580
Maybe she switched boyfriends.

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:55.680
N-No way!

00:16:57.500 --> 00:16:58.790
Are you handsome?

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:00.120
Rich?

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:01.800
Own a car?

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.050
Cheerful?

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:07.830
There, you see?

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:09.370
It's no contest.

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:11.530
Godai wins!

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:14.710
It'll never happen.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:35.060
How are Godai and Kozue
getting along?

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:39.030
Why do you ask?

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:43.230
I saw Kozue the other day.

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:50.270
You rascal, you!

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:54.180
Stole Godai's girlfriend,
didn't you?

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:58.920
And now you want to know if their
relationship is fallin' apart?

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:01.310
What're you saying?!

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:05.950
Oh, come now!
As if you didn't know!

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:10.730
Someone saw you with
Kozue in your arms.

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:15.360
It's a misunderstanding!
Kozue and I aren't...!

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:16.490
Mr. Mitaka!

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:37.950
Godai never smiles when we
see each other anymore.

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:41.770
I wish he'd at least put his arm
around me when we say goodbye.

00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:45.150
What am I doing?!

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:59.240
A struggling student,
Lying in the chilly draft
Too poor to shiver.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:01.010
Time to hit the sack.

00:19:57.940 --> 00:20:00.930
Miss Otanashi, would you join
me for tea on the way home?

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:03.170
She's here again.

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:00.900
All right, Kozue,
I understand.

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:03.930
Just leave everything to me.

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:06.230
Mr. Mitaka
that's wonderful!

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:09.300
I have to use the ladies room.

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:14.770
I'll have to settle this
face-to-face with Godai.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:21.620
I hope this isn't just
a game for you!

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:23.540
Godai!

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:26.450
You'd better be serious
about her.

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:27.890
What're you saying?!

00:21:28.130 --> 00:21:30.720
It's your fault that all
this happened!

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:34.430
If you're a man, at least
give Kozue a goodbye hug!

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:35.900
Got that?!

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:38.590
I'll be going now.

00:21:40.310 --> 00:21:45.110
In a relationship, it's how
you say goodbye that counts.

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:47.370
Wait!

00:21:55.260 --> 00:21:56.590
How you say goodbye...?

00:21:58.960 --> 00:21:59.940
What're you...?

00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:05.530
Godai.

00:22:10.880 --> 00:22:13.780
It's how you say goodbye
that counts?

00:22:14.780 --> 00:22:16.830
That was a surprise!

00:22:17.350 --> 00:22:19.280
When did the two of you
switch places?

00:22:19.920 --> 00:22:22.880
He's right... If we're
going to break up anyway...

00:22:41.940 --> 00:22:45.000
It was fun, Kozue.

00:22:47.650 --> 00:22:48.440
Goodbye.

00:22:55.620 --> 00:22:59.210
I'm so happy!
You finally understand!

00:23:00.430 --> 00:23:02.290
Goodbye!
See you again!

00:23:04.360 --> 00:23:05.520
See you again?

00:23:07.300 --> 00:23:07.890
Huh?!

00:23:49.810 --> 00:23:51.740
The day is Christmas Eve.

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:56.750
A stone brings a flurry of
romance to Chachamaru!

00:23:57.150 --> 00:24:01.140
Next: "Love Takes Guts!
Godai's Part-Time Gambit"

00:24:01.520 --> 00:24:05.980
It's our Christmas story,
part one.
